        "original_id": "d1684e5a-dcbb-5918-b72a-bb7b5defde79",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts, Danielle Brooks\n- Works: Violet, Chinglish, From Up Here, The Ugliest Pilgrim, The Color Purple, Orange Is the New Black\n- Roles: stage director, actress\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley.\n- Violet is based on the short story The Ugliest Pilgrim by Doris Betts.\n- In 2008, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- In 2011, the comedy play Chinglish opened on Broadway with direction by Leigh Silverman.\n- In 2014, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.\n- In 2015, Danielle Brooks received a Tony Award nomination for portraying Sofia in the Broadway production of The Color Purple.\n- Danielle Brooks is best known for playing Tasha \"Taystee\" Jefferson on the Netflix original series Orange Is the New Black.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
